      "behavior_quotes": [
        "With sugarRushSlowsTime enabled, an Added event for a Player with SugarRush passes ceil(float(nativeDuration)*2F) and the same2F to enterSlowMotion. ServerLevel-only helper searches Citadel LocalEntityTickRateModifiers by entity ID; the first matching modifier has only maxDuration updated, then returns. Otherwise it submits a new modifier with original player ID/type, third double argument10D, current dimension, supplied duration and supplied float. Exact Citadel2.7.6 proves radius10 and multiplier2 with maxDuration in master ticks; the five-contract dependency registry records the exact applicability, configured hook limits and transport. Expiration requests leaveSlowMotion only for Player/SugarRush/configtrue; explicit Remove has only the original exit sound, no leave call. Dimension travel requests leave whenever the Player still has SugarRush, without a config check or destination substitution. Leave searches the full list and removes only the last matching local modifier. No new type/rate/dimension filter is added to either search. Player RETURN injections with configtrue, SugarRush and native proxy-active gate multiply original getSpeed by3F; getFlyingSpeed returns this.getSpeed()*0.5F rather than multiplying original flying speed. Native proxy compares server tick-length return with50 or client tracker return with50F. isTimeModificationValid returnsfalse only for a LocalEntityTickRateModifier when this Player lacks SugarRush. Exact dependency controller resolves player validity, strict radius and duration/rate transport. LOCAL_ENTITY alone leaves server tick-length50, so this native server proxy gate is false for SugarRush alone. The active Citadel client Pre tick writes a200ms query for one valid multiplier2 (local factor appears twice); inactive server/entity mixins are not inferred into effective server slowdown. Native update/remove does not sync existing client copies. Native original potion definitions supply {'potion_regular_duration': 1800, 'potion_long_duration': 3600} to this existing effect holder; native potion delivery/lifecycle retains original source admission. No duplicate effect callback. Shared proxy tick-rate query uses Citadel ServerTickRateTracker.getServerTickLengthMs()!=50/server and ClientTickRateTracker.getClientTickRate()!=50F/client. These native API queries and ClientEvents hand-pose clock are independently captured. Exact Citadel2.7.6 execution and configured-hook limits are resolved in alexscaves-citadel-dependency-obligations.json; this native protocol refinement supplies no second speed/duration formula."
